# Paired Route: Mining + Blacksmithing 1-300 (WoW: Forever)
# Follows docs/MULTI_PROFESSION_RULES.md:
# - Dedicated per-combination file: guides/pairs/mining-blacksmithing.guide
# - Single-anchor sections on Blacksmithing (crafting anchor) in rising order
#   so Polestar's section auto-skip and remaining-material subtraction work;
#   Mining trainers, skill checkpoints and smelting tips are interleaved
#   inside each Blacksmithing bracket.
# - The Blacksmithing recipes, bands, spell ids and material counts come
#   straight from guides/blacksmithing.guide; the Mining trainers and
#   node loops come from guides/mining.guide (NPC ids, coordinates and the
#   Mining pick id were resolved from the Forever reference data there).
# - Every `collect ... gather Mining <rank>` has a matching `auction` goal
#   in the same section, with the same gather ranks the solo Blacksmithing
#   guide uses, so Mix / Gather / Buy modes all work.
# - Smelting is described in tips, not as craft steps: smelting also raises
#   Mining skill, so pick whichever of mining or smelting suits you.
# - Forever scarce drops (looked up with polestar find): Pyrite (Alchemy
#   Sulfuric Acid 249410), Bauxite (Engineering Sandpaper 249432) and
#   Pitchblende 249426 (Mining Azerothium Bar 249726, with Coal).
#   Sulfuric Acid and Sandpaper are made by other professions, so this
#   route points at the Auction House for them rather than assuming an alt.
# - Original prose for this pack; external data sources keep their licenses.
#
# Mining-to-Blacksmithing skill map:
#   Blacksmithing 1-50    Mining 1-65     copper veins, Rough Stone
#   Blacksmithing 50-100  Mining 65-100   tin and silver, Bronze and Silver Bars
#   Blacksmithing 100-140 Mining 125      iron, Heavy Stone
#   Blacksmithing 140-175 Mining 175      iron bars, gold, Arathi
#   Blacksmithing 175-225 Mining 200-245  mithril and truesilver
#   Blacksmithing 225-300 Mining 275-300  thorium, Pitchblende
guide forever-professions/pair-mining-blacksmithing
title Mining + Blacksmithing 1-300
category Professions
folder Paired Routes
coords era
levels 1-60
zone Azeroth
keywords mining, blacksmithing, paired, ore, pitchblende

pitch Level Mining and Blacksmithing together from 1 to 300: dig the ore, smelt it into bars and stone, and hammer it into plate.
pro Mine and smelt nearly every stone and bar the Blacksmithing route needs, so there is very little Auction House spending
pro Gets you Pitchblende and the Azerothium Bar at 300, plus the Pyrite and Bauxite that other crafters want
con Uses both primary profession slots, and the Thorium bars for the last 100 points take a lot of mining

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice

section Blacksmithing 1-50

step Learn Blacksmithing
  only Alliance
  zone Ironforge
  tip Blacksmithing and Mining take both of your primary profession slots. Groum Stonebeard in Ironforge teaches Apprentice Blacksmithing at any character level. Buy a Blacksmith Hammer now: most recipes need one in your bags.
  train Blacksmithing Apprentice npc 10277

step Learn Blacksmithing
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Blacksmithing and Mining take both of your primary profession slots. Ug'thok in Orgrimmar teaches Apprentice Blacksmithing at any character level. Buy a Blacksmith Hammer now: most recipes need one in your bags.
  train Blacksmithing Apprentice npc 10266

step Learn Mining and Buy a Pick
  only Alliance
  zone Ironforge
  tip Geofram Bouldertoe in Ironforge teaches Apprentice Mining at any character level, and the capital trainer teaches every later rank too. Buy a Mining Pick: it stays in your bags and does not need to be equipped, but you cannot mine without one. Switch on Find Minerals from the Mining box of the Professions window (it is off by default and resets when you die; you can track minerals or herbs, not both). Mining also yields the Scarce drops Pyrite, Bauxite and Pitchblende.
  train Mining Apprentice npc 4254
  buy 2901 x1 nearest

step Learn Mining and Buy a Pick
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Makaru in Orgrimmar teaches Apprentice Mining at any character level, and the capital trainer teaches every later rank too. Buy a Mining Pick: it stays in your bags and does not need to be equipped, but you cannot mine without one. Switch on Find Minerals from the Mining box of the Professions window (it is off by default and resets when you die; you can track minerals or herbs, not both). Mining also yields the Scarce drops Pyrite, Bauxite and Pitchblende.
  train Mining Apprentice npc 3357
  buy 2901 x1 nearest

step Blacksmithing 1-50: tools
  tip A Blacksmith Hammer from any Blacksmithing supply vendor, usually next to the trainer. Keep it in your bags: most recipes need it.
  buy 5956 x1 nearest

step Copper in Elwynn Forest
  only Alliance
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip Mine every Copper Vein and Poor Copper Vein you pass until Mining 65; Poor Copper Veins give Copper Ore and Rough Stone from skill 1. The Rough Stone is what Blacksmithing 1-50 eats, so keep all of it. Hold on to the Copper Ore too: smelted into Copper Bars it becomes your Bronze Bars at 75 and 125. Stop at a forge in Goldshire to smelt.
