step Blacksmithing 1-50: Auction House
  tip What the first stones take that the Auction House sells: 90 Rough Stone. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 2835 x90

step Blacksmithing 1-50: stone
  tip Rough Stone comes from Copper Veins while mining. You should already hold plenty from the copper loop above, or take it from your bank.
  collect 2835 x90 anywhere gather Mining 1

step Rough Sharpening Stone, Rough Grinding Stone (1-50)
  tip Rough Sharpening Stone, 30 crafts to 25, then Rough Grinding Stone, 30 crafts to 50: two Rough Stone in each of the second. Keep 10 of the grinding stones: the Silver Rods at 75 need them. Both are taught with Apprentice Blacksmithing.
  learn 2660 "Rough Sharpening Stone"
  craft 2660 "Rough Sharpening Stone" until 25
  learn 3320 "Rough Grinding Stone"
  craft 3320 "Rough Grinding Stone" until 50

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Journeyman

section Blacksmithing 50-75

step Journeyman Blacksmithing
  only Alliance
  zone Ironforge
  tip Journeyman Blacksmithing raises the cap to 150; it needs skill 50 and character level 10. Rotgath Stonebeard in Ironforge teaches it. Train now: the next recipe is taught from 50.
  level 10
  train Blacksmithing Journeyman npc 10276

step Journeyman Blacksmithing
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Journeyman Blacksmithing raises the cap to 150; it needs skill 50 and character level 10. Snarl in Orgrimmar teaches it. Train now: the next recipe is taught from 50.
  level 10
  train Blacksmithing Journeyman npc 1383

step Journeyman Mining
  only Alliance
  zone Ironforge
  tip Journeyman Mining raises the Mining cap to 150 and needs skill 50. Geofram Bouldertoe is in the same city, so do both trainers on one trip. Tin Veins need Mining 65 and Silver Veins 75.
  train Mining Journeyman npc 4254

step Journeyman Mining
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Journeyman Mining raises the Mining cap to 150 and needs skill 50. Makaru is in the same city, so do both trainers on one trip. Tin Veins need Mining 65 and Silver Veins 75.
  train Mining Journeyman npc 3357

step Tin and Incendicite in the Wetlands
  only Alliance
  zone Wetlands
  tip The Wetlands cave is full of Tin Veins and Incendicite Mineral Veins and regrows quickly; the mobs inside are around level 20, so outlevel them a little. Keep every Tin Vein's Coarse Stone for this band and every Silver Vein's ore for the Silver Rods. Smelt your Copper and Tin into Bronze, and Silver Ore into Silver Bars, before you leave: Smelt Bronze stops giving skill points around 105.
  goto 47.5,62.1 "Incendicite Mineral Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 48.9,59.3 "Incendicite Mineral Vein" r 30
  goto 51.3,58.6 "Incendicite Mineral Vein, Copper Vein" r 30
  goto 51.2,61.6 "Incendicite Mineral Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 47.3,66.4 "Incendicite Mineral Vein, Copper Vein" r 30
  goto 24.0,60.0 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 25.8,50.2 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 27.8,38.0 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  skill Mining 100

step Tin in Hillsbrad Foothills
  only Horde
  zone Hillsbrad Foothills
  tip Hillsbrad Foothills is the best open route for this band and it is popular, so expect company near Tarren Mill. Keep every Tin Vein's Coarse Stone for this band and every Silver Vein's ore for the Silver Rods. Smelt your Copper and Tin into Bronze, and Silver Ore into Silver Bars, before you leave: Smelt Bronze stops giving skill points around 105. The Barrens and Ashenvale are quieter alternatives.
  goto 31.5,57.5 "Tin Vein, Silver Vein" r 30
  goto 27.6,57.5 "Tin Vein, Silver Vein" r 30
  goto 31.4,52.7 "Tin Vein, Silver Vein" r 30
  goto 40.7,53.4 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 38.5,63.8 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 17.1,56.3 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 21.8,40.9 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  skill Mining 100

step Blacksmithing 50-75: Auction House
  tip What the next stones take that the Auction House sells: 72 Coarse Stone. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 2836 x72

step Blacksmithing 50-75: stone
  tip Coarse Stone comes from Tin Veins while mining. You should already hold plenty from the tin loop above, or take it from your bank.
  collect 2836 x72 anywhere gather Mining 65

step Coarse Grinding Stone (50-75)
  tip Coarse Grinding Stone, 36 crafts to 75: two Coarse Stone in each. Make all 36 and keep them: 10 go into the bracers at 95 and 26 into the bracers at 112.
  learn 3326 "Coarse Grinding Stone"
  craft 3326 "Coarse Grinding Stone" until 75

section Blacksmithing 75-100

step Blacksmithing 75-100: Auction House
  tip What the next pieces take that the Auction House sells: 5 Silver Bar, 115 Bronze Bar. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 2842 x5
  auction 2841 x115

step Blacksmithing 75-100: bars
  tip Smelt Silver at a forge for the Silver Bars (Silver Ore, Mining 75). Smelt Bronze from one Copper Bar and one Tin Bar (Mining 65): smelt the Copper Ore first, then the Tin. Smelting raises Mining as well, so it is free skill if you are still under 125. Smelt your own ore, or take the bars from your bank.
  collect 2842 x5 anywhere gather Mining 75
  collect 2841 x115 anywhere gather Mining 65

step Silver Rod, Rough Bronze Leggings, Patterned Bronze Bracers (75-100)
  tip Silver Rod, 5 crafts to 80: a Silver Bar and two of the kept Rough Grinding Stones each. Then Rough Bronze Leggings, 15 crafts to 95. Then Patterned Bronze Bracers, 5 crafts to 100: five Bronze Bars and two of the kept Coarse Grinding Stones each. If one Silver Bar costs more than 10 Copper Bars, make Runed Copper Belts instead of the rods (10 Copper Bars each).
  learn 7818 "Silver Rod"
  craft 7818 "Silver Rod" x5
  learn 2668 "Rough Bronze Leggings"
  craft 2668 "Rough Bronze Leggings" until 95
  learn 2672 "Patterned Bronze Bracers"
  craft 2672 "Patterned Bronze Bracers" until 100

section Blacksmithing 100-125

step Tin and Iron toward Mining 125 (Alliance)
  only Alliance
  zone Wetlands
  tip Finish Mining 125 on the same Wetlands loop; Iron Deposits open at 125, and Heavy Stone is dropped only by Iron Deposits. Keep the ore for Bronze Bars, since this band and the shortsword band both want Bronze.
  goto 20.7,35.2 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 34.1,15.2 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 43.6,22.6 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 44.5,41.7 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  skill Mining 125

step Tin and Iron toward Mining 125 (Horde)
  only Horde
  zone Hillsbrad Foothills
  tip Finish Mining 125 on the same Hillsbrad loop; Iron Deposits open at 125, and Heavy Stone is dropped only by Iron Deposits. Keep the ore for Bronze Bars, since this band and the shortsword band both want Bronze.
  goto 26.2,31.8 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 37.5,25.9 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 39.0,36.7 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 54.9,23.7 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  goto 13.5,79.2 "Copper Vein, Tin Vein" r 30
  skill Mining 125

step Blacksmithing 100-125: Auction House
  tip What the next pieces take that the Auction House sells: 60 Heavy Stone, 65 Bronze Bar. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 2838 x60
  auction 2841 x65

step Blacksmithing 100-125: stone and bars
  tip Heavy Stone comes from Iron Deposits while mining; Bronze Bar is smelted from a Copper Bar and a Tin Bar. Iron Deposits are rare in the Wetlands and Hillsbrad, so top up at Arathi Highlands in the next band if you come up short, or take them from your bank.
  collect 2838 x60 anywhere gather Mining 125
  collect 2841 x65 anywhere gather Mining 65

step Heavy Grinding Stone, Patterned Bronze Bracers (100-125)
  tip Heavy Grinding Stone, 20 crafts to 112: three Heavy Stone in each. Keep all 20: the Golden Scale Bracers at 180 need them. Then Patterned Bronze Bracers, 13 more crafts to 125, using the last 26 kept Coarse Grinding Stones.
  learn 3337 "Heavy Grinding Stone"
  craft 3337 "Heavy Grinding Stone" until 112
  craft 2672 "Patterned Bronze Bracers" until 125

section Blacksmithing 125-140

step Blacksmithing 125-140: Auction House
  tip What the shortswords take that the Auction House sells: 120 Bronze Bar, 48 Medium Leather. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 2841 x120
  auction 2319 x48

step Blacksmithing 125-140: bars and leather
  tip Bronze Bar is smelted from a Copper Bar and a Tin Bar; Medium Leather is skinned from beasts in the 15-30 zones. Gather them while you level, or take them from your bank. If you still hold loose Copper and Tin Ore, smelt it now, since Bronze needs both in equal numbers.
  collect 2841 x120 anywhere gather Mining 65
  collect 2319 x48 anywhere gather Skinning 100

step Blacksmithing 125-140: vendor goods
  tip Weak Flux comes from the Blacksmithing supply vendor next to the trainer in every capital city.
  buy 2880 x96 nearest

step Bronze Shortsword (125-140)
  tip Bronze Shortsword, 24 crafts to 140: five Bronze Bars, four Weak Flux and two Medium Leather each. They sell to vendors for more than twice the bracers, so the route is cheaper overall. Disenchanters can make Patterned Bronze Bracers instead (120 Bronze Bar, 48 Coarse Grinding Stone).
  learn 2742 "Bronze Shortsword"
  craft 2742 "Bronze Shortsword" until 140

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Expert

section Blacksmithing 140-175

step Expert Blacksmithing
  only Alliance
  zone Ironforge
  tip Expert Blacksmithing raises the cap to 225; it needs skill 125 and character level 20, and costs 50 silver. Bengus Deepforge in Ironforge teaches it. Train before crafting the bracers: no skill above 150 without it.
  level 20
  train Blacksmithing Expert npc 4258

step Expert Blacksmithing
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Expert Blacksmithing raises the cap to 225; it needs skill 125 and character level 20, and costs 50 silver. Saru Steelfury in Orgrimmar teaches it. Train before crafting the bracers: no skill above 150 without it.
  level 20
  train Blacksmithing Expert npc 3355

step Expert Mining
  only Alliance
  zone Ironforge
  tip Expert Mining raises the Mining cap to 225 and needs skill 125. Geofram Bouldertoe teaches it in the same city as your Blacksmithing trainer. Without it, Mining stalls at 150 and you cannot mine Gold or Mithril.
  train Mining Expert npc 4254

step Expert Mining
  only Horde
  zone Orgrimmar
  tip Expert Mining raises the Mining cap to 225 and needs skill 125. Makaru teaches it in the same city as your Blacksmithing trainer. Without it, Mining stalls at 150 and you cannot mine Gold or Mithril.
  train Mining Expert npc 3357

step Iron and Gold in Arathi Highlands
  zone Arathi Highlands
  tip Iron Deposits need 125 and Gold Veins 155; this band burns 240 Iron Bar, so mine a lot of Iron Ore. Arathi Highlands has four caves worth going all the way into: you will not see every vein from the entrance. Low-level characters should skip the caves and work the open ground south of Hammerfall, or try Thousand Needles. Smelt Iron to Iron Bars as you go; at 155 Smelt Gold is useful skill if prices are kind. Keep any Pyrite and Bauxite you get: Sulfuric Acid and Sandpaper both feed later Blacksmithing recipes.
  goto 19.2,93.3 "Tin Vein, Gold Vein" r 30
  goto 28.4,88.2 "Tin Vein, Gold Vein" r 30
  goto 26.8,69.6 "Tin Vein, Gold Vein" r 30
  goto 15.8,63.2 "Tin Vein, Iron Deposit" r 30
  goto 17.3,47.7 "Tin Vein, Iron Deposit" r 30
  goto 39.6,73.1 "Tin Vein, Gold Vein" r 30
  goto 48.3,64.4 "Tin Vein, Gold Vein" r 30
  goto 57.7,73.3 "Tin Vein, Gold Vein" r 30
  goto 69.1,82.7 "Tin Vein, Gold Vein" r 30
  goto 48.6,85.2 "Tin Vein, Gold Vein" r 30
  goto 78.8,43.6 "Tin Vein, Gold Vein" r 30
  goto 29.1,15.2 "Tin Vein, Gold Vein" r 30
  skill Mining 175

step Blacksmithing 140-175: Auction House
  tip What the bracers take that the Auction House sells: 240 Iron Bar. The counts drop by what your bags, bank and mail hold.
  auction 3575 x240

step Blacksmithing 140-175: bars
  tip Iron Bar is smelted from Iron Ore (Mining 125) at any forge: Smelt Iron is a quick skill gain on the way past 125. Smelt your own ore, or take the bars from your bank.
  collect 3575 x240 anywhere gather Mining 125

step Blacksmithing 140-175: vendor goods
  tip Green Dye comes from Tamar in Orgrimmar and Bombus Finespindle in Ironforge, and from other dye vendors.
  buy 2605 x40 nearest

step Green Iron Bracers (140-175)
  tip Green Iron Bracers, 40 crafts to 175: six Iron Bars and a Green Dye each.
  learn 3501 "Green Iron Bracers"
  craft 3501 "Green Iron Bracers" until 175

section Blacksmithing 175-195

step Mithril in the Hinterlands
  zone The Hinterlands
  tip Mithril Deposits need Mining 175, which you now have. The Hinterlands loop is the pick for this band: mine Mithril for the Solid Stone, Mithril Bars and Citrine the next three brackets burn. Skip the stretch with level 62 elites, and lower levels may want to skip the cave. Keep every Pyrite, Bauxite and Pitchblende that drops: it is Scarce and worth far more than the stone it comes with. Tanaris is the alternative zone, but its caves are for level 60s.
  goto 20.8,58.8 "Mithril Deposit, Truesilver Deposit" r 30
  goto 25.1,68.8 "Mithril Deposit, Truesilver Deposit" r 30
  goto 33.3,60.6 "Mithril Deposit, Truesilver Deposit" r 30
  goto 41.0,66.1 "Mithril Deposit, Truesilver Deposit" r 30
